It is a Go port of algovoi-rfc9421-verifier (Python/TypeScript reference
implementations) and reproduces the reference signing-base construction,
Signature-Input/Signature parsing, Ed25519 public-key gate, and Content-Digest
and freshness checks byte-for-byte. The separate ecdsa add-on package provides
the RFC 9421 ecdsa-p256-sha256 and ecdsa-p384-sha384 verifiers and depends on the
core package (the core never depends on the add-on).

The canonicalisation discipline (urn:x402:canonicalisation:jcs-rfc8785-v1) is
specified in IETF Internet-Draft draft-hopley-x402-canonicalisation-jcs-v1 and
documented at https://docs.algovoi.co.uk/canonicalisation-substrate.

